# Multiperspective Digital Libraries: The Implications of Constructionism for the Development of Digital Libraries.

**Authors:** Tuominen, Kimmo, Talja, Sanna, Savolainen, Reijo

## Abstract
Highlights the importance of conceptual and theoretical work in designing information retrieval systems. Examines two epistemological positions leading to different solutions in digital library design: the information transfer perspective and the social constructionist knowledge production perspective. Suggests that noun-based approaches can be replaced by adding verbs to visualize the structure of conversations. (Contains 54 references.) (Author/LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ671880

